---
smd: 2
title: Includes in spec v2
summary: "Pins proposal 9: with smd: 2, :::include section= matches a heading's id, or its whole text in any case, and never a part of it. include-terms.smd says smd: 1, but the including document's version decides."
status: draft
updated: 2026-10-17
---

## By heading text

The whole text of a heading, in any case, with its subsections:

:::include{file="include-terms.smd" section="PRICING" level=3}
See [Pricing](include-terms.smd#pricing) in the shared terms.
:::

## By heading id

:::include{file="include-terms.smd" section="#refunds" level=3}
See [Refunds](include-terms.smd#refunds) in the shared terms.
:::

## A part of a heading's text

In spec v1 `section="refund"` finds "Refunds". In spec v2 it names no heading, so the fallback shows:

<!-- smd-disable-next-line include/missing-section -->
:::include{file="include-terms.smd" section="refund"}
The refund policy is in [the shared terms](include-terms.smd#refunds).
:::
